# Agent OS

Read [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) for the full map. Follow it on every task.

## Sources of truth (do not duplicate)

- Behavior/UX → [`PRODUCT.md`](PRODUCT.md) (read relevant §§; do not copy into rules)
- Seeded-launch implementation (phases/locks) → [`LAUNCH.md`](LAUNCH.md)
- As-built system → [`ARCHITECTURE.md`](ARCHITECTURE.md)
- Shortcomings → [`gaps/`](gaps/) + [`gaps/CLUSTERS.md`](gaps/CLUSTERS.md)
- Future bets / brainstorm → [`ideas/`](ideas/) (not committed behavior; not gaps)
- HTTP contract → [`openapi.json`](openapi.json)

## Working norms (summary)

Deep investigate before coding (proportional to risk). Evidence-driven; say when guessing. Clean UX + full correctness. File gaps for holes. Prefer **parallel subagents** for forked POVs — then **always verify** their findings against the codebase/PRODUCT before acting. Product/UX forks → stop and ask.

## Definition of done (behavior changes)

1. [`.agents/skills/simplify-pass/SKILL.md`](.agents/skills/simplify-pass/SKILL.md)
2. `./scripts/ci-local.sh` green (includes Playwright E2E)
3. **Stop** — no commit/push unless the user explicitly asks
4. Stress E2E ×N only if asked

## Hard stops (ask first)

PRODUCT/UX/behavior changes · Railway/Meta/Resend mutations · un-parking parked gaps · secrets / `.cursor/mcp.json`
